## 7. Live

| | |
|---|---|
| App | https://rail-pay.vercel.app |
| Chat | https://t.me/RailpayBot |
| Provider | https://rail-pay.vercel.app/provider |
| Relayer | https://rail-pay-production.up.railway.app |
| Code | https://github.com/lozentrad3s/rail |

Monad testnet, chain 10143. Addresses in `docs/DEPLOYMENTS.md`.

### Trying it

**As a sender:** open the app, set up with Face ID, tap **Add $10,000 practice money**. In the chat,
`add mum` (or dad, or a friend), choose **Test Bank (test mode only)** and any account number, then
`send 50k to mum` and approve on your phone. Your dashboard shows it running, then delivered.

**As a provider:** `/provider`, sign in with Dynamic (wallet or email), get test AUSD and MON, stake
at least $100. Requests appear live with a suggested bid from your margin; turn on alerts, or say
`alerts` to the Telegram bot.

---

## 8. What is not finished

- **CRE is simulated, not deployed.** Deployment needs Early Access; a relay key carries the DON's
  verdict to Monad until there is a forwarder.
- **The pilot's provider payouts are simulated.** The two bots record the transfer they would have
  made; no naira moves.
- **WhatsApp is pending Meta's business verification.** The transport is built and tested.
- **Paystack is in test mode**, which permits three live bank resolves per day. Hence the test bank.
- **No audit.** Testnet, practice money, and nobody should put real savings behind it yet.

---

*Rail is not another fintech promising a better rate. It is the mechanism that makes providers
compete for every transfer, in the open, and hands the difference back to the person who sent it.*
